 "summary": "The name of this Act is the House of Representatives Member Election (First Amendment) Act, 2083 (Section 1, Subsection 1, Page 1). The main purpose of this Act is to amend the House of Representatives Member Election Act, 2074 by replacing Schedule-1 relating to the inclusive basis for the closed list of candidates (Preamble, Page 1; Section 2, Page 1). This Act shall come into force immediately (Section 1, Subsection 2, Page 1).\n\nThis Act repeals the House of Representatives Member Election (First Amendment) Ordinance, 2082 (Section 3, Subsection 1, Page 2). Any acts and actions done pursuant to that repealed Ordinance shall be deemed to have been done pursuant to this Act (Section 3, Subsection 2, Page 2).",
